Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["13. Notes on rigor and limitations", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"96589397-bbe8-c341-9e03-13ad1988d475"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"WorkingPrecision", "->", "Infinity"}]], "InlineWL", "Input",
  ShowAutoStyles->True,
  ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
  LanguageCategory->"Input",
  ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee64269c-e8f6-9f4a-9a5a-c81433eeb822"],
 " is ",
 StyleBox["not a valid executable numerical setting",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " in built-in numerical functions. In practice, use arbitrarily high but \
finite precision where needed."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a5467bcd-4883-6a44-9959-f991d13b5322"],

Cell["\<\
Exact symbolic derivation is preferred first; then finite-dimensional \
spectral reduction; then high-precision numerics.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3fcfc911-8319-d344-ae47-321fedb54e9e"],

Cell["\<\
If you want a fully coupled nonlinear framework, the next step is to specify \
the exact field operator beyond the closure heuristic so that residual \
minimization is mathematically well posed.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4cb79e14-7452-5348-a757-e025c1f0e9f0"],

