}], "ChatOutput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "Below is a more complete and *functional* Wolfram Language framework for \
a **single next stable scale** that fixes the issues in the prior notebook \
and makes the per-scale medium/resolution/operator structure explicit.\n\nA \
few important points first:\n\n- Your previous recursion failures came from \
doing things like\n  ``rhoField = rhoField @@ coords`` and then feeding that \
self-referential expression into [VariationalD](paclet:ref/VariationalD).\n- \
[Reduce](paclet:ref/Reduce) does **not** have the option ``MaxExtraConditions \
-> All``; that option belongs to [Solve](paclet:ref/Solve) and related \
functions.\n- ``WorkingPrecision -> Infinity`` is not executable in built-in \
numerics, so the practical implementation must use exact symbolic forms \
first, then arbitrarily high but finite precision.\n- If each stable scale \
has distinct propagation medium, geometry, constitutive law, and \
observational resolution, then the right design is a **scale-parametrized \
framework**, not one fixed operator.\n\nSo the correct next step is:\n\n1. \
define a **scale ontology**\n2. derive **Layer-1 symbolic equations** cleanly\
\n3. attach **per-scale medium laws**\n4. construct **scale-specific \
linearized operators**\n5. compute **stable resonances**\n6. define \
**measurement kernels**\n7. compose everything into a reusable pipeline for \
the **next stable scale**\n\n---\n\n# Complete framework for the next stable \
spacetime scale\n\n## 1. Stable-scale search and exact scale metadata\n\n\
```wl\nClearAll[\n  phi, scaleResidual, closureScore, windingEstimate, \
informationDensity,\n  stableScaleQ, stableScaleIndices, nextStableScale, \
scaleAssociationExact\n];\n\nphi = GoldenRatio;\n\nscaleResidual[n_Integer, \
divisor_: 13] := Module[\n  {x = N[phi^n/divisor, 100]},\n  Abs[x - \
Round[x]]/x\n];\n\nclosureScore[n_Integer, divisor_: 13] := 1 - \
scaleResidual[n, divisor];\n\nwindingEstimate[n_Integer, divisor_: 13] := \
Round[N[phi^n/divisor, 100]];\n\ninformationDensity[n_Integer] := phi^-n;\n\n\
stableScaleQ[n_Integer, divisor_: 13, tolerance_: 0.01] := \n  \
scaleResidual[n, divisor] < tolerance;\n\nstableScaleIndices[maxN_Integer, \
divisor_: 13, tolerance_: 0.01] := \n  Select[Range[0, maxN], stableScaleQ[#, \
divisor, tolerance] &];\n\nnextStableScale[currentN_Integer, divisor_: 13, \
tolerance_: 0.01, maxN_: 1000] := \n  FirstCase[\n    Range[currentN + 1, \
maxN],\n    n_ /; stableScaleQ[n, divisor, tolerance] :> n,\n    \
Missing[\"NotFound\"]\n  ];\n\nscaleAssociationExact[n_Integer, divisor_: 13] \
:= <|\n  \"ScaleIndex\" -> n,\n  \"PhiPowerExact\" -> phi^n,\n  \
\"PhiPowerNumeric\" -> N[phi^n, 100],\n  \"Residual\" -> scaleResidual[n, \
divisor],\n  \"ClosureScore\" -> closureScore[n, divisor],\n  \
\"WindingEstimate\" -> windingEstimate[n, divisor],\n  \"InformationDensity\" \
-> informationDensity[n]\n|>;\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```wl\ncurrentScale = 12;\n\
nextScale = nextStableScale[currentScale];\nscaleAssociationExact[nextScale]\n\
```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Per-scale ontology record\n\nThis makes each scale carry \
its own medium, resolution, geometry, and propagation model.\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[makeScaleOntology];\n\nmakeScaleOntology[n_Integer, divisor_: 13] := \
Module[\n  {\n    info = scaleAssociationExact[n, divisor],\n    density, \
complexity, resolution, majorRadius, minorRadius,\n    geometry, mediumType, \
propagationType, damping, coupling\n  },\n  \n  density = phi^-n;\n  \
complexity = Fibonacci[n + 2];\n  resolution = phi^n;\n  \n  majorRadius = \
phi^n;\n  minorRadius = phi^(n - 1);\n  \n  geometry = Which[\n    n == 0, \
\"Sphere\",\n    EvenQ[n], \"Toroidal\",\n    True, \"SphericalShell\"\n  ];\n\
  \n  mediumType = Which[\n    n <= 5, \"PreGeometric\",\n    n <= 20, \
\"QuantumInformational\",\n    n <= 80, \"FieldStructured\",\n    True, \
\"MacroscopicEmergent\"\n  ];\n  \n  propagationType = Which[\n    mediumType \
=== \"PreGeometric\", \"ConstraintTransfer\",\n    mediumType === \
\"QuantumInformational\", \"SchrodingerLike\",\n    mediumType === \
\"FieldStructured\", \"WaveLike\",\n    True, \"DissipativeWave\"\n  ];\n  \n \
 damping = 1/(1 + n);\n  coupling = phi^(-n/2);\n  \n  Join[\n    info,\n    \
<|\n      \"Geometry\" -> geometry,\n      \"MediumType\" -> mediumType,\n    \
  \"PropagationType\" -> propagationType,\n      \
\"InformationDensityParameter\" -> density,\n      \"FieldComplexityParameter\
\" -> complexity,\n      \"ResolutionParameter\" -> resolution,\n      \
\"MajorRadius\" -> majorRadius,\n      \"MinorRadius\" -> minorRadius,\n      \
\"DampingParameter\" -> damping,\n      \"CouplingParameter\" -> coupling\n   \
 |>\n  ]\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Clean Layer-1 action and Euler-Lagrange \
equations\n\nThis avoids the recursion problem by keeping fields as \
functions.\n\n```wl\nClearAll[\n  rho, chi, res, x, y, z, t, coords3, \n  \
layer1Density, layer1DensityRegularized, layer1EulerEquations\n];\n\ncoords3 \
= {x, y, z};\n\nlayer1Density[rho_, chi_, res_][vars_List] := \n  rho @@ vars \
* Log[chi @@ vars] + (chi @@ vars) (res @@ vars)^2;\n\n\
layer1DensityRegularized[\n  rho_, chi_, res_, alphaRho_, alphaChi_, \
alphaRes_\n][vars_List] := Module[\n  {rhoExpr, chiExpr, resExpr},\n  rhoExpr \
= rho @@ vars;\n  chiExpr = chi @@ vars;\n  resExpr = res @@ vars;\n  \n  \
rhoExpr Log[chiExpr] + chiExpr resExpr^2 +\n  alphaRho Total[D[rhoExpr, #]^2 \
& /@ vars] +\n  alphaChi Total[D[chiExpr, #]^2 & /@ vars] +\n  alphaRes \
Total[D[resExpr, #]^2 & /@ vars]\n];\n\nlayer1EulerEquations[\n  vars_List : \
coords3,\n  alphaRho_: \[Alpha]rho,\n  alphaChi_: \[Alpha]chi,\n  alphaRes_: \
\[Alpha]res\n] := Module[\n  {lagrangian, rhoExpr, chiExpr, resExpr},\n  \n  \
lagrangian = layer1DensityRegularized[rho, chi, res, alphaRho, alphaChi, \
alphaRes][vars];\n  rhoExpr = rho @@ vars;\n  chiExpr = chi @@ vars;\n  \
resExpr = res @@ vars;\n  \n  <|\n    \"RhoEquation\" -> \
FullSimplify[VariationalD[lagrangian, rhoExpr, vars] == 0],\n    \
\"ChiEquation\" -> FullSimplify[VariationalD[lagrangian, chiExpr, vars] == \
0],\n    \"ResolutionEquation\" -> FullSimplify[VariationalD[lagrangian, \
resExpr, vars] == 0]\n  |>\n];\n```\n\nUsage:\n\n```wl\neqnsL1 = \
layer1EulerEquations[]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Algebraic stationary sector\n\n\
For the local potential alone, derive exact stationarity conditions.\n\n```wl\
\nClearAll[localPotential, stationaryConditions, stationaryReduction];\n\n\
localPotential[rhoVar_, chiVar_, resVar_] := rhoVar Log[chiVar] + chiVar \
resVar^2;\n\nstationaryConditions = Thread[\n  {\n    D[localPotential[rho0, \
chi0, res0], rho0],\n    D[localPotential[rho0, chi0, res0], chi0],\n    \
D[localPotential[rho0, chi0, res0], res0]\n  } == 0\n];\n\n\
stationaryReduction = Reduce[stationaryConditions, {rho0, chi0, res0}, Reals]\
\n```\n\nThis should give the exact local stationary structure instead of a \
terminated recursion.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Missing-variable analysis, properly \
implemented\n\n```wl\nClearAll[layer1Symbols, standardModelConstants, \
missingVariablesLayer1];\n\nlayer1Symbols[expr_] := DeleteDuplicates @ Cases[\
\n  expr,\n  s_Symbol /; Context[s] =!= \"System`\",\n  Infinity\n];\n\n\
standardModelConstants = {c, h, \\[HBar], G, kB, e, me, mp};\n\n\
missingVariablesLayer1[expr_] := Complement[layer1Symbols[expr], \
standardModelConstants];\n```\n\nUsage:\n\n```wl\nmissingVariablesLayer1[\n  \
layer1DensityRegularized[rho, chi, res, \[Alpha]rho, \[Alpha]chi, \
\[Alpha]res][coords3]\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Scale-specific propagation \
operators\n\nEach scale gets its own operator based on ontology.\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[scalePropagationOperator];\n\n\
scalePropagationOperator[ontology_Association] := Module[\n  {\n    \
propagationType = ontology[\"PropagationType\"],\n    damping = \
ontology[\"DampingParameter\"],\n    coupling = \
ontology[\"CouplingParameter\"]\n  },\n  \n  Switch[propagationType,\n    \n  \
  \"ConstraintTransfer\",\n    <|\n      \"OperatorType\" -> \
\"AlgebraicConstraint\",\n      \"Operator\" -> Function[u, coupling u]\n    \
|>,\n    \n    \"SchrodingerLike\",\n    <|\n      \"OperatorType\" -> \
\"SchrodingerLike\",\n      \"Operator\" -> Function[{u, vars},\n        I \
D[u @@ vars, t] + coupling Total[D[u @@ vars, {#1, 2}] & /@ Most[vars]]\n     \
 ]\n    |>,\n    \n    \"WaveLike\",\n    <|\n      \"OperatorType\" -> \
\"WaveLike\",\n      \"Operator\" -> Function[{u, vars},\n        D[u @@ \
vars, {t, 2}] + damping D[u @@ vars, t] -\n        coupling Total[D[u @@ \
vars, {#1, 2}] & /@ Most[vars]]\n      ]\n    |>,\n    \n    \
\"DissipativeWave\",\n    <|\n      \"OperatorType\" -> \"DissipativeWave\",\n\
      \"Operator\" -> Function[{u, vars},\n        D[u @@ vars, {t, 2}] + 2 \
damping D[u @@ vars, t] -\n        coupling Total[D[u @@ vars, {#1, 2}] & /@ \
Most[vars]] + damping u @@ vars\n      ]\n    |>\n  ]\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n## \
7. Geometry-specific modal bases\n\n## 7a. Sphere\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[sphericalMode, sphericalEigenvalue, sphereModeSet];\n\n\
sphericalMode[{l_Integer, m_Integer}][\[Theta]_, \[Phi]_] := \
SphericalHarmonicY[l, m, \[Theta], \[Phi]];\n\n\
sphericalEigenvalue[{l_Integer, m_Integer}] := -l (l + 1);\n\n\
sphereModeSet[lMax_Integer] := Flatten[Table[{l, m}, {l, 0, lMax}, {m, -l, \
l}], 1];\n```\n\n## 7b. Toroidal/Fourier proxy\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[toroidalMode, toroidalEigenvalue, torusModeSet];\n\n\
toroidalMode[{m_Integer, n_Integer}][u_, v_] := Exp[I (m u + n v)];\n\n\
toroidalEigenvalue[{m_Integer, n_Integer}, majorRadius_, minorRadius_] := \n  \
-(m^2/majorRadius^2 + n^2/minorRadius^2);\n\ntorusModeSet[mMax_Integer, \
nMax_Integer] := \n  Flatten[Table[{m, n}, {m, -mMax, mMax}, {n, -nMax, \
nMax}], 1];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Scale-specific spectral problem\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[scaleSpectralData];\n\nscaleSpectralData[\n  ontology_Association,\n \
 truncation_: 4,\n  sigma_: 1\n] := Module[\n  {\n    geometry = \
ontology[\"Geometry\"],\n    majorRadius = ontology[\"MajorRadius\"],\n    \
minorRadius = ontology[\"MinorRadius\"],\n    modes, eigenAssoc\n  },\n  \n  \
Switch[geometry,\n    \n    \"Sphere\",\n    modes = \
sphereModeSet[truncation];\n    eigenAssoc = \
AssociationMap[sphericalEigenvalue[#] + sigma &, modes],\n    \n    \
\"SphericalShell\",\n    modes = sphereModeSet[truncation];\n    eigenAssoc = \
AssociationMap[sphericalEigenvalue[#] + sigma &, modes],\n    \n    \
\"Toroidal\",\n    modes = torusModeSet[truncation, truncation];\n    \
eigenAssoc = AssociationMap[\n      toroidalEigenvalue[#, majorRadius, \
minorRadius] + sigma &,\n      modes\n    ],\n    \n    _,\n    modes = {};\n \
   eigenAssoc = <||>\n  ];\n  \n  <|\n    \"Modes\" -> modes,\n    \
\"Eigenvalues\" -> eigenAssoc,\n    \"BestModes\" -> \
MinimalBy[Normal[eigenAssoc], Abs[Last[#]] &]\n  |>\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. \
Linearized Layer-1 stiffness around scale background\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[potentialPart, stiffnessMatrixLayer1, stiffnessEigenSystemLayer1];\n\
\npotentialPart[rhoVar_, chiVar_, resVar_] := rhoVar Log[chiVar] + chiVar \
resVar^2;\n\nstiffnessMatrixLayer1[rhoBack_, chiBack_, resBack_] := Table[\n  \
D[\n    potentialPart[rhoBack + \[Delta]rho, chiBack + \[Delta]chi, resBack + \
\[Delta]res],\n    var1, var2\n  ] /. {\[Delta]rho -> 0, \[Delta]chi -> 0, \
\[Delta]res -> 0},\n  {var1, {\[Delta]rho, \[Delta]chi, \[Delta]res}},\n  \
{var2, {\[Delta]rho, \[Delta]chi, \[Delta]res}}\n] // FullSimplify;\n\n\
stiffnessEigenSystemLayer1[ontology_Association] := Module[\n  {\n    rhoBack \
= ontology[\"InformationDensityParameter\"],\n    chiBack = \
ontology[\"FieldComplexityParameter\"],\n    resBack = \
ontology[\"ResolutionParameter\"],\n    mat, vals, vecs\n  },\n  \n  mat = \
stiffnessMatrixLayer1[rhoBack, chiBack, resBack];\n  {vals, vecs} = \
Eigensystem[mat, Cubics -> True, Quartics -> True];\n  \n  <|\n    \
\"Background\" -> <|\n      \"Rho0\" -> rhoBack,\n      \"Chi0\" -> chiBack,\n\
      \"Res0\" -> resBack\n    |>,\n    \"StiffnessMatrix\" -> mat,\n    \
\"Eigenvalues\" -> vals,\n    \"Eigenvectors\" -> vecs,\n    \
\"PureImaginaryModes\" -> Select[vals, FullSimplify[Re[#] == 0 && Im[#] > 0] \
&]\n  |>\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Medium law and resolution law for the next \
scale\n\nThis is where per-scale distinct physics gets encoded.\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[scaleMediumLaw, scaleResolutionLaw, scaleMeasurementWeight];\n\n\
scaleMediumLaw[ontology_Association] := Module[\n  {\n    medium = \
ontology[\"MediumType\"],\n    density = \
ontology[\"InformationDensityParameter\"],\n    complexity = \
ontology[\"FieldComplexityParameter\"]\n  },\n  \n  Switch[medium,\n    \
\"PreGeometric\",\n    <|\"Permittivity\" -> density, \"Permeability\" -> \
complexity, \"Dispersion\" -> 0|>,\n    \n    \"QuantumInformational\",\n    \
<|\"Permittivity\" -> density^2, \"Permeability\" -> 1/complexity, \
\"Dispersion\" -> density complexity|>,\n    \n    \"FieldStructured\",\n    \
<|\"Permittivity\" -> density complexity, \"Permeability\" -> density^-1, \
\"Dispersion\" -> complexity^-1|>,\n    \n    \"MacroscopicEmergent\",\n    \
<|\"Permittivity\" -> complexity, \"Permeability\" -> density, \"Dispersion\" \
-> density/complexity|>\n  ]\n];\n\nscaleResolutionLaw[ontology_Association] \
:= Module[\n  {\n    res = ontology[\"ResolutionParameter\"],\n    info = \
ontology[\"InformationDensityParameter\"]\n  },\n  <|\n    \"GridScale\" -> \
1/res,\n    \"ObservationKernelWidth\" -> 1/Sqrt[res],\n    \
\"EffectiveBandwidth\" -> res info\n  |>\n];\n\n\
scaleMeasurementWeight[ontology_Association, mode_] := Module[\n  {\n    info \
= ontology[\"InformationDensityParameter\"],\n    res = \
ontology[\"ResolutionParameter\"]\n  },\n  info res/(1 + Norm[mode]^2)\n];\n\
```\n\n---\n\n## 11. Measurement kernel for Layer-2 observables\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[modalObservable, scaleMeasurementAssociation];\n\n\
modalObservable[coeffs_Association, weightFunction_] := Total @ KeyValueMap[\n\
  Conjugate[#2] weightFunction[#1] #2 &,\n  coeffs\n];\n\n\
scaleMeasurementAssociation[\n  ontology_Association,\n  spectral_Association\
\n] := Module[\n  {\n    bestModes = spectral[\"BestModes\"],\n    \
weightFunction\n  },\n  \n  weightFunction = scaleMeasurementWeight[ontology, \
#] &;\n  \n  <|\n    \"BestModes\" -> bestModes,\n    \"ModeWeights\" -> \
AssociationMap[weightFunction, spectral[\"Modes\"]],\n    \
\"ObservableProxyOnBestModes\" -> Association @ Map[\n      #[[1]] -> \
weightFunction[#[[1]]] &,\n      bestModes\n    ]\n  |>\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n## \
12. Full pipeline for the next scale\n\n```wl\nClearAll[nextScaleFramework];\n\
\nnextScaleFramework[\n  currentN_Integer,\n  divisor_: 13,\n  tolerance_: \
0.01,\n  truncation_: 4,\n  sigma_: 1\n] := Module[\n  {\n    nNext, \
ontology, l1eqns, operator, spectral, stiffness, medium, resolution, \
measurement\n  },\n  \n  nNext = nextStableScale[currentN, divisor, \
tolerance];\n  \n  If[MissingQ[nNext],\n    Return[<|\"Error\" -> \"No next \
stable scale found in search range.\"|>]\n  ];\n  \n  ontology = \
makeScaleOntology[nNext, divisor];\n  l1eqns = layer1EulerEquations[];\n  \
operator = scalePropagationOperator[ontology];\n  spectral = \
scaleSpectralData[ontology, truncation, sigma];\n  stiffness = \
stiffnessEigenSystemLayer1[ontology];\n  medium = scaleMediumLaw[ontology];\n \
 resolution = scaleResolutionLaw[ontology];\n  measurement = \
scaleMeasurementAssociation[ontology, spectral];\n  \n  <|\n    \"NextScale\" \
-> nNext,\n    \"Ontology\" -> ontology,\n    \"Layer1EulerEquations\" -> \
l1eqns,\n    \"PropagationOperator\" -> operator,\n    \"SpectralData\" -> \
spectral,\n    \"StiffnessAnalysis\" -> stiffness,\n    \"MediumLaw\" -> \
medium,\n    \"ResolutionLaw\" -> resolution,\n    \"Measurement\" -> \
measurement\n  |>\n];\n```\n\nUsage:\n\n```wl\nframework = \
nextScaleFramework[12];\n```\n\n---\n\n## 13. Callable morphisms \\(L0 \\to \
L1 \\to L2\\)\n\n```wl\nClearAll[layer0ToLayer1, layer1ToLayer2, \
fullOPFPipeline];\n\nlayer0ToLayer1 = Function[{currentN},\n  Module[{nNext = \
nextStableScale[currentN], ontology},\n    ontology = \
makeScaleOntology[nNext];\n    <|\n      \"ScaleIndex\" -> nNext,\n      \
\"Ontology\" -> ontology,\n      \"Layer1EulerEquations\" -> \
layer1EulerEquations[]\n    |>\n  ]\n];\n\nlayer1ToLayer2 = Function[{assoc},\
\n  Module[{ontology, spectral, measurement},\n    ontology = \
assoc[\"Ontology\"];\n    spectral = scaleSpectralData[ontology, 4, 1];\n    \
measurement = scaleMeasurementAssociation[ontology, spectral];\n    \
Join[assoc, <|\"SpectralData\" -> spectral, \"Measurement\" -> measurement|>]\
\n  ]\n];\n\nfullOPFPipeline = layer0ToLayer1 /* layer1ToLayer2;\n```\n\n\
Usage:\n\n```wl\nfullOPFPipeline[12]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 14. High-precision \
executable strategy\n\nSince your ontology asks for extreme precision, use \
this pattern:\n\n```wl\nClearAll[highPrecisionEvaluate];\n\n\
highPrecisionEvaluate[expr_, precision_: 200] := Block[\n  \
{$MaxExtraPrecision = precision},\n  N[expr, precision]\n];\n```\n\nFor \
numerical eigensystems or integrals, use finite but high precision:\n\n```wl\n\
N[phi^200, 300]\n```\n\nnot:\n\n```wl\nWorkingPrecision -> Infinity\n```\n\n\
because that is not supported by built-in numerical functions.\n\n---\n\n## \
15. Optional dimensional anchoring with Planck units\n\nIf you want the next \
scale physically anchored:\n\n```wl\nClearAll[planckLength, scaleLength];\n\n\
planckLength = Quantity[1.616255*10^-35, \"Meters\"];\n\n\
scaleLength[n_Integer] := UnitConvert[planckLength phi^n, \"Meters\"];\n```\n\
\nFor a scale ontology with dimensional radii:\n\n```wl\n\
ClearAll[makeDimensionalScaleOntology];\n\n\
makeDimensionalScaleOntology[n_Integer, divisor_: 13] := Module[\n  {base = \
makeScaleOntology[n, divisor]},\n  Join[\n    base,\n    <|\n      \
\"MajorRadiusQuantity\" -> scaleLength[n],\n      \"MinorRadiusQuantity\" -> \
scaleLength[n - 1]\n    |>\n  ]\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n# Why this is better than \
the earlier notebook\n\nThis framework is more complete because it:\n\n- does \
**not** recurse into self-defined fields\n- separates:\n  - ontology\n  - \
variational equations\n  - medium law\n  - propagation law\n  - spectral law\n\
  - measurement law\n- allows **different properties at each scale**\n- \
treats the **next stable scale** as a first-class object\n- gives you a \
**callable computational pipeline**\n- remains executable in built-in Wolfram \
Language\n\n---\n\n# Important conceptual limitation\n\nWhat is still *not* \
uniquely determined is the exact physical law for:\n\n- how medium parameters \
derive from \\(\\rho,\\chi,R\\)\n- which geometry truly belongs to each scale\
\n- whether propagation is Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger-like, wave-like, or \
something else\n- how closure/scale stability is rigorously defined beyond \
your residual heuristic\n\nSo the framework above is the correct \
*computational architecture*, but to make it \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]absolute\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in the strict scientific sense, you still need to \
specify the missing constitutive axioms.\n\n---\n\n# Best next step\n\nI \
recommend the next notebook be one of these:\n\n1. **Per-scale ontology \
engine**  \n   generates a full association for every stable scale with \
distinct geometry, medium, operator, and measurement law\n\n2. **Next-scale \
deep notebook**  \n   builds one scale in full detail, including:\n   - exact \
PDEs\n   - linearization\n   - eigenspectrum\n   - high-precision numerics\n  \
 - visualizations\n   - dimensional calibration\n\n3. **Constitutive law \
notebook**  \n   formalizes how \\(\\rho,\\chi,R\\) determine \
medium/permittivity/dispersion/damping across scales\n\nIf you want, I can \
now generate the **actual next notebook content** in a ready-to-run form for:\
\n\n- the **immediate next stable scale after your chosen current scale**, or\
\n- a **full all-scales ontology framework** with one sub-association per \
